0016 regrid-old-fine-face-period (Role 3 -> Role 1). Against committed Source/driver/RegistryTransfer.cpp (HEAD 65983d4189; unchanged since 41329dd277).
Apply from the repo root: git apply 0016-regrid-old-fine-face-period.patch
RegistryTransfer::prolong (the driver's regrid path, fill_remade_level) copies the old fine face velocities onto the new fine level without the fine periodicity:
a new fine box on one copy of a periodic domain face (x = N) whose old data lies on the other copy (x = 0) keeps the coarse prolongation there, while the x = 0 copy
holds the old fine values -> the two copies differ, the cells next to the seam carry a div error that the post-regrid projection cannot remove (one phi, two face values).
Same fix as fdsrt::prolong_faces_level (regrid_transport commit, `period` argument).

